# Literature Review on Algorithmic Trading in Financial Markets

**Authors:** Vaibhav Aggarwal, Shallu Batra, Mahender Yadav, Pankaj Kumar

## Abstract
The financial market has drastically changed because of technological development. One of the most critical developments in this area is algorithmic trading, which refers to using computers to execute transactions. The role of algorithmic trading in financial markets has increased exponentially over the last decade; however, a literature review is scant. In this study, we aim to plug this research gap. We initially retrieved 2007 articles from the Scopus database using a defined search string. Keeping this research to the subject confined and selecting only articles from prestigious journals, 30 articles are selected for this review. This study highlights that the existing study highly emphasized the effect of algorithmic trading on liquidity, volatility, investors' emotions, and the discovery of stock prices. Furthermore, some future guidelines are also suggested through this review.

